1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:01,268
Day 61 starts fifty

2
00:00:01,268 --> 00:00:03,562
steps from a red fuel can.

3
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:05,311
You spent the whole night right here,

4
00:00:05,311 --> 00:00:07,077
on the bank beside the track,

5
00:00:07,077 --> 00:00:09,045
because neither of you would walk toward it,

6
00:00:09,045 --> 00:00:11,386
and neither of you would turn your back on it.

7
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:14,139
The circles glowed until morning.

8
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:15,288
Pair after pair,

9
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:17,953
along the rails, into the country.

10
00:00:18,328 --> 00:00:19,870
Patient as streetlights.

11
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:22,206
At dawn, you walk up to the can.

12
00:00:22,661 --> 00:00:25,174
Up close, it's just a can.

13
00:00:25,174 --> 00:00:26,256
Dented,

14
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:28,799
empty, a little rust around the cap.

15
00:00:29,461 --> 00:00:30,859
Mara says again that

16
00:00:30,859 --> 00:00:32,390
it isn't the same one.

17
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:34,622
You say again that you don't know.

18
00:00:34,622 --> 00:00:35,555
It's the most honest

19
00:00:35,555 --> 00:00:37,226
conversation you've had all week.

20
00:00:37,226 --> 00:00:38,743
So you do what you always do

21
00:00:38,743 --> 00:00:40,978
with something you don't understand.

22
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:42,166
You test it.

23
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,292
You take the roll of tape from your

24
00:00:44,292 --> 00:00:46,914
bag and wind one strip around the handle.

25
00:00:46,914 --> 00:00:49,907
Then you write on the tape in pencil,

26
00:00:49,907 --> 00:00:51,550
as small as you can.

27
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:52,163
61.

28
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,220
If you ever see this can again,

29
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,197
you'll know.

30
00:00:55,909 --> 00:00:58,569
Down the track, the lit circles wait.

31
00:00:58,569 --> 00:00:59,730
Back on day 31,

32
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:01,536
you stepped off their road,

33
00:01:01,536 --> 00:01:05,027
and the lights went out behind you, one by one.

34
00:01:05,027 --> 00:01:07,485
So you climb the bank into the field,

35
00:01:07,485 --> 00:01:10,194
slowly, so Mara's ankle can keep up.

36
00:01:10,536 --> 00:01:12,166
At the top, you look back.

37
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:14,374
The circles are still lit.

38
00:01:14,374 --> 00:01:15,121
All of them.

39
00:01:15,121 --> 00:01:17,418
On the road, the lights gave up on you.

40
00:01:17,418 --> 00:01:18,752
These ones don't.

41
00:01:19,286 --> 00:01:21,452
That night, you sleep under a stone

42
00:01:21,452 --> 00:01:24,784
bridge where a country lane crosses a stream.

43
00:01:24,784 --> 00:01:26,645
You open the tin and write:

44
00:01:26,645 --> 00:01:29,038
they left the lights on.

45
00:01:29,038 --> 00:01:29,856
By day 63,

46
00:01:29,856 --> 00:01:35,154
you've learned exactly how far a sprained ankle goes in a day.

47
00:01:35,154 --> 00:01:36,211
Not far.

48
00:01:36,601 --> 00:01:37,982
You walk the field edges,

49
00:01:37,982 --> 00:01:40,672
keeping a hedge between you and the railway.

50
00:01:41,094 --> 00:01:42,442
Mara won't lean on you.

51
00:01:42,442 --> 00:01:45,122
She leans on a stick she found instead,

52
00:01:45,122 --> 00:01:47,751
and tells you it's a much better listener.

53
00:01:48,318 --> 00:01:51,045
At midday, the hedge ends at a canal.

54
00:01:51,045 --> 00:01:52,423
Flat brown water,

55
00:01:52,423 --> 00:01:55,993
a towpath along one side, and nobody on it.

56
00:01:55,993 --> 00:01:58,413
Tied to two iron rings is a long,

57
00:01:58,413 --> 00:01:59,573
narrow boat,

58
00:01:59,573 --> 00:02:02,651
painted green, with a little chimney on its roof.

59
00:02:02,651 --> 00:02:04,634
You watch it for an hour.

60
00:02:04,634 --> 00:02:06,206
Nothing moves except a duck,

61
00:02:06,206 --> 00:02:08,597
and the duck isn't interested in you.

62
00:02:08,597 --> 00:02:10,797
The cabin door is unlocked.

63
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:13,091
Inside, there are two narrow bunks,

64
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:15,144
a small iron wood stove,

65
00:02:15,144 --> 00:02:17,217
a dented kettle, and a cupboard.

66
00:02:17,217 --> 00:02:20,205
You open the cupboard like it might bite.

67
00:02:20,205 --> 00:02:22,052
Between what's in there and what's

68
00:02:22,052 --> 00:02:25,155
left in your bags, you count eleven tins,

69
00:02:25,155 --> 00:02:28,619
half a bag of rice, and a jar of honey.

70
00:02:28,619 --> 00:02:29,873
You count it twice.

71
00:02:29,873 --> 00:02:31,616
It doesn't get bigger,

72
00:02:32,054 --> 00:02:33,998
but it doesn't get smaller either,

73
00:02:33,998 --> 00:02:36,321
which these days counts as good news.

74
00:02:36,321 --> 00:02:38,974
The boat's water tank is empty.

75
00:02:38,974 --> 00:02:41,170
The canal is right outside,

76
00:02:41,170 --> 00:02:43,167
brown and full of leaves.

77
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:46,271
Mara says you're boiling every drop of it.

78
00:02:46,271 --> 00:02:48,847
You shake the last gas canister.

79
00:02:48,847 --> 00:02:50,443
It barely makes a sound.

80
00:02:50,443 --> 00:02:53,012
You write it down on the roll.

81
00:02:53,012 --> 00:02:53,421
Boat.

82
00:02:53,421 --> 00:02:54,879
Until the ankle.

83
00:02:55,573 --> 00:02:58,581
Mara reads it, and adds a line underneath.

84
00:02:58,581 --> 00:03:00,521
Not one day longer.

85
00:03:00,521 --> 00:03:01,808
On day 66,

86
00:03:01,808 --> 00:03:04,923
the gas runs out in the middle of a kettle.

87
00:03:04,923 --> 00:03:07,020
The blue flame shrinks to a ring,

88
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,321
then a dot, then nothing.

89
00:03:09,855 --> 00:03:11,069
The water is warm,

90
00:03:11,069 --> 00:03:14,279
but it isn't boiled, and warm isn't good enough.

91
00:03:14,279 --> 00:03:16,366
So it's the wood stove now.

92
00:03:16,837 --> 00:03:19,088
There's a box of matches in the cupboard.

93
00:03:19,088 --> 00:03:22,365
Before you strike one, you count them.

94
00:03:22,365 --> 00:03:22,788
Thirty-two.

95
00:03:22,788 --> 00:03:24,766
Wood is easy.

96
00:03:24,766 --> 00:03:26,540
The hedges are full of dead branches.

97
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,393
The chimney is the problem.

98
00:03:28,393 --> 00:03:29,788
A fire makes smoke,

99
00:03:29,788 --> 00:03:32,948
and smoke is the most obvious thing you could

100
00:03:32,948 --> 00:03:35,001
possibly hang over your own heads.

101
00:03:35,001 --> 00:03:37,006
They notice what changes.

102
00:03:37,006 --> 00:03:38,495
You wrote that on day 18.

103
00:03:38,495 --> 00:03:40,797
So you only light the stove after dark,

104
00:03:40,797 --> 00:03:42,052
when a thin gray line

105
00:03:42,052 --> 00:03:44,339
against a black sky is hard to see.

106
00:03:44,339 --> 00:03:46,299
Mara keeps the kettle going.

107
00:03:46,299 --> 00:03:47,679
You lie on the roof and

108
00:03:47,679 --> 00:03:48,638
watch the chimney,

109
00:03:48,638 --> 00:03:51,057
the dark, and the railway beyond the field.

110
00:03:51,057 --> 00:03:54,103
The first night, nothing happens.

111
00:03:54,103 --> 00:03:55,594
Neither does the second.

112
00:03:55,594 --> 00:03:56,906
On the third morning,

113
00:03:56,906 --> 00:03:58,631
you open the cabin door.

114
00:03:58,631 --> 00:04:00,944
Fifty steps along the towpath,

115
00:04:00,944 --> 00:04:04,231
standing by itself, is a red fuel can.

116
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:06,864
There's tape around its handle.

117
00:04:06,864 --> 00:04:07,742
On the tape,

118
00:04:07,742 --> 00:04:11,794
in tiny pencil, in your handwriting: 61.

119
00:04:12,474 --> 00:04:14,656
Mara doesn't say it isn't the same can.

120
00:04:14,656 --> 00:04:16,560
She doesn't say anything at all.

121
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,125
Somewhere along the way,

122
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:21,553
it stopped mattering whether it came from the station.

123
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:22,535
It's yours now.

124
00:04:22,535 --> 00:04:23,756
You signed it.

125
00:04:24,356 --> 00:04:27,904
On day 69, you stop guessing and ask.

126
00:04:27,904 --> 00:04:31,142
Something wrote in your ledger on day 45.

127
00:04:31,677 --> 00:04:33,704
It seems only fair to write back.

128
00:04:33,704 --> 00:04:35,710
You don't know if it can read.

129
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:36,792
So you draw.

130
00:04:36,792 --> 00:04:39,047
At the end of the roll,

131
00:04:39,047 --> 00:04:41,924
you draw the stadium bowl, as well as you can remember it.

132
00:04:41,924 --> 00:04:43,297
Little figures walking in.

133
00:04:43,297 --> 00:04:44,565
Then a question mark big

134
00:04:44,565 --> 00:04:46,836
enough that nobody could miss it.

135
00:04:46,836 --> 00:04:49,028
Mara adds two stick figures beside it.

136
00:04:49,028 --> 00:04:50,624
One with a scarf.

137
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:52,045
One with a band on its arm.

138
00:04:52,045 --> 00:04:53,568
She says if you're going to ask,

139
00:04:53,568 --> 00:04:55,795
you might as well say who's asking.

140
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,014
You set the tin on top of

141
00:04:57,014 --> 00:04:59,003
the red can and go back inside.

142
00:04:59,003 --> 00:04:59,595
At dusk,

143
00:04:59,595 --> 00:05:02,477
the plain figure comes along the towpath.

144
00:05:02,477 --> 00:05:02,969
Alone.

145
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:05,238
It doesn't even look at the boat.

146
00:05:05,238 --> 00:05:06,896
It goes straight to the can,

147
00:05:06,896 --> 00:05:08,283
lifts the tin,

148
00:05:08,283 --> 00:05:11,174
and unrolls the paper across its gloved hand.

149
00:05:11,174 --> 00:05:13,608
It looks at your drawing for a long time.

150
00:05:13,608 --> 00:05:15,508
Then it takes something thin from

151
00:05:15,508 --> 00:05:17,693
its case and bends over the roll.

152
00:05:17,693 --> 00:05:18,721
When it leaves,

153
00:05:18,721 --> 00:05:20,901
you make yourself wait an hour.

154
00:05:20,901 --> 00:05:21,847
Then you run.

155
00:05:21,847 --> 00:05:24,274
Under your question, there's a map.

156
00:05:24,274 --> 00:05:25,491
Thin, perfect lines,

157
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:28,177
much neater than anything you've ever drawn.

158
00:05:28,177 --> 00:05:30,509
A small square for the station.

159
00:05:30,509 --> 00:05:31,545
Then the drain,

160
00:05:31,545 --> 00:05:35,597
the store, the signal hut, the stone bridge, this boat.

161
00:05:35,597 --> 00:05:37,068
Even the bus shelter.

162
00:05:37,068 --> 00:05:38,716
Even the hedge.

163
00:05:38,716 --> 00:05:40,401
Every place you've slept,

164
00:05:40,401 --> 00:05:42,802
in order, joined by one long line.

165
00:05:42,802 --> 00:05:44,895
It didn't answer your question.

166
00:05:44,895 --> 00:05:46,708
It answered the one you've

167
00:05:46,708 --> 00:05:48,451
been carrying since day 60.

168
00:05:48,451 --> 00:05:49,871
Who expected you?

169
00:05:50,278 --> 00:05:51,027
It did.

170
00:05:51,027 --> 00:05:52,898
Every single night.

171
00:05:52,898 --> 00:05:55,073
At the very end of the line,

172
00:05:55,073 --> 00:05:57,671
past the boat, there's one more mark.

173
00:05:57,671 --> 00:05:58,669
A tall,

174
00:05:58,669 --> 00:06:01,079
thin line with a small triangle on top.

175
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:03,400
Beside it, two joined circles.

176
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,334
You climb onto the roof.

177
00:06:05,692 --> 00:06:08,111
On the ridge where the railway disappears,

178
00:06:08,111 --> 00:06:09,932
small against the sky,

179
00:06:09,932 --> 00:06:11,238
there's a radio mast.

180
00:06:11,238 --> 00:06:12,781
You've been looking at it

181
00:06:12,781 --> 00:06:14,945
all week without seeing it.

182
00:06:14,945 --> 00:06:15,740
On day 72,

183
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:18,346
you need to know how it finds you.

184
00:06:18,346 --> 00:06:19,799
If it follows your things,

185
00:06:19,799 --> 00:06:22,027
you can leave your things behind.

186
00:06:22,027 --> 00:06:23,026
Even the tin.

187
00:06:23,026 --> 00:06:24,539
Mara hates this.

188
00:06:24,928 --> 00:06:27,488
She hated it on day 45, too.

189
00:06:27,974 --> 00:06:29,718
But if it follows you,

190
00:06:29,718 --> 00:06:31,913
then no hedge, no drain,

191
00:06:32,446 --> 00:06:34,975
and no boat will ever hide you again.

192
00:06:35,524 --> 00:06:36,605
So before dawn,

193
00:06:36,605 --> 00:06:39,675
you leave everything you carry on the boat.

194
00:06:39,675 --> 00:06:40,414
The bags,

195
00:06:40,414 --> 00:06:43,234
the tin, the map, even the pencil.

196
00:06:43,234 --> 00:06:45,094
Then you cross the field and

197
00:06:45,094 --> 00:06:46,916
lie flat in a ditch,

198
00:06:46,916 --> 00:06:49,249
with nothing in your hands but grass.

199
00:06:49,249 --> 00:06:51,228
The striped figure comes

200
00:06:51,228 --> 00:06:52,787
along the towpath at sunrise.

201
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:53,983
The plain figure walks

202
00:06:53,983 --> 00:06:55,815
behind it with its case.

203
00:06:55,815 --> 00:06:56,844
The scanner rises.

204
00:06:56,844 --> 00:06:59,312
The pale line goes through the boat.

205
00:06:59,312 --> 00:07:00,732
Across the bunks.

206
00:07:00,732 --> 00:07:02,151
Across your bags.

207
00:07:02,151 --> 00:07:03,453
Across the tin.

208
00:07:03,453 --> 00:07:04,713
It doesn't stop.

209
00:07:04,713 --> 00:07:06,639
It comes out the far side

210
00:07:06,639 --> 00:07:08,254
and starts across the field.

211
00:07:08,254 --> 00:07:10,626
You press your face into the ground.

212
00:07:10,626 --> 00:07:12,774
The line touches your back.

213
00:07:12,774 --> 00:07:13,650
And stops.

214
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:14,825
Six seconds.

215
00:07:15,424 --> 00:07:18,195
Then it moves to Mara, and stops again.

216
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:21,073
The striped figure steps off the towpath,

217
00:07:21,073 --> 00:07:22,367
toward the ditch.

218
00:07:22,982 --> 00:07:24,366
It's the first time one of them

219
00:07:24,366 --> 00:07:26,267
has ever come toward you on purpose.

220
00:07:26,673 --> 00:07:27,917
Then the plain figure kneels

221
00:07:27,917 --> 00:07:29,589
and sets something on the path.

222
00:07:29,963 --> 00:07:31,052
A small marker.

223
00:07:31,052 --> 00:07:33,665
Two circles, joined by a short line.

224
00:07:34,055 --> 00:07:35,443
The striped figure stops.

225
00:07:35,443 --> 00:07:37,292
It looks down at the marker.

226
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:38,852
Then it turns away,

227
00:07:38,852 --> 00:07:40,454
and they leave together.

228
00:07:41,181 --> 00:07:43,307
You lie in that ditch long after they're gone,

229
00:07:43,307 --> 00:07:45,570
because you've seen this before.

230
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:46,448
Day one.

231
00:07:46,448 --> 00:07:48,981
The scanner stopped.

232
00:07:48,981 --> 00:07:50,857
The striped figure turned away.

233
00:07:50,857 --> 00:07:53,273
The other one placed a marker.

234
00:07:53,273 --> 00:07:54,194
For seventy-one days,

235
00:07:54,194 --> 00:07:57,350
you've believed it stopped on a bottle.

236
00:07:57,350 --> 00:07:58,780
It was never the bottle.

237
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:01,165
Mara says the marker is a label.

238
00:08:01,165 --> 00:08:02,355
Already counted.

239
00:08:02,355 --> 00:08:03,405
Leave these two.

240
00:08:03,405 --> 00:08:05,011
You say it looked more

241
00:08:05,011 --> 00:08:06,612
like somebody stepping in.

242
00:08:06,612 --> 00:08:07,977
You can't decide which

243
00:08:07,977 --> 00:08:09,939
one you'd rather believe.

244
00:08:09,939 --> 00:08:13,101
That night, Mara writes in the ledger.

245
00:08:13,101 --> 00:08:13,823
It sees us.

246
00:08:13,823 --> 00:08:16,576
She doesn't write theory next to it.

247
00:08:16,576 --> 00:08:18,449
You add two words underneath.

248
00:08:18,449 --> 00:08:19,752
Since day one.

249
00:08:20,752 --> 00:08:21,381
On day 75,

250
00:08:21,381 --> 00:08:23,977
Mara takes the tape off her ankle.

251
00:08:23,977 --> 00:08:25,293
It's still a little swollen,

252
00:08:25,293 --> 00:08:27,154
but it holds her weight, and she makes a

253
00:08:27,154 --> 00:08:29,670
point of standing on it in front of you.

254
00:08:29,670 --> 00:08:30,616
Along the towpath,

255
00:08:30,616 --> 00:08:33,707
there's an old apple tree that nobody has picked.

256
00:08:33,707 --> 00:08:35,655
You fill both bags and feel

257
00:08:35,655 --> 00:08:38,004
richer than you have since the station.

258
00:08:38,004 --> 00:08:38,960
Mara counts the

259
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,684
apples out loud on the roof.

260
00:08:41,684 --> 00:08:42,060
Twenty-six.

261
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:43,687
From up there,

262
00:08:43,687 --> 00:08:45,837
you can see the railway, one field away.

263
00:08:45,837 --> 00:08:47,105
In the afternoon,

264
00:08:47,463 --> 00:08:49,733
two people come walking along the track.

265
00:08:49,733 --> 00:08:50,897
Away from the city.

266
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:52,072
Toward the ridge.

267
00:08:52,072 --> 00:08:53,797
They carry one bag each,

268
00:08:53,797 --> 00:08:57,739
and the circles glow ahead of them, one pair at a time.

269
00:08:57,739 --> 00:08:59,563
Mara stands up on the roof.

270
00:08:59,563 --> 00:09:01,324
You know what she's going to do

271
00:09:01,324 --> 00:09:04,043
before she does it, and you don't stop her.

272
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:05,002
She calls out.

273
00:09:05,002 --> 00:09:07,717
Her voice carries across the whole field,

274
00:09:07,717 --> 00:09:09,345
louder than anything either

275
00:09:09,345 --> 00:09:11,444
of you has said in seventy-five days.

276
00:09:11,444 --> 00:09:13,859
One of them stops and turns.

277
00:09:13,859 --> 00:09:14,763
For a moment,

278
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:17,937
that stranger and Mara just look at each other.

279
00:09:17,937 --> 00:09:20,436
Then the stranger raises an arm.

280
00:09:20,436 --> 00:09:20,897
Waves.

281
00:09:20,897 --> 00:09:22,542
Turns back to the track,

282
00:09:22,542 --> 00:09:24,092
and keeps walking.

283
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:27,196
The lights lead them on, toward the mast.

284
00:09:27,196 --> 00:09:28,923
Mara keeps her arm up long

285
00:09:28,923 --> 00:09:30,827
after there's nobody to see it.

286
00:09:30,827 --> 00:09:32,158
That evening,

287
00:09:32,158 --> 00:09:35,775
she writes under her old line from day 33.

288
00:09:35,775 --> 00:09:37,433
We called out.

289
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:40,225
Underneath, smaller: they waved.

290
00:09:40,838 --> 00:09:41,447
On day 78,

291
00:09:41,447 --> 00:09:43,760
the sky behind you has an edge again.

292
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:46,657
You see it from the roof, first thing.

293
00:09:46,657 --> 00:09:49,065
Eighteen days ago, the ship was a

294
00:09:49,065 --> 00:09:50,952
dark wall lying along the horizon.

295
00:09:50,952 --> 00:09:52,168
Now it's taller.

296
00:09:52,525 --> 00:09:53,945
Its straight edge reaches a

297
00:09:53,945 --> 00:09:55,467
quarter of the way up the sky,

298
00:09:55,467 --> 00:09:57,415
and its shadow lies across the fields

299
00:09:57,415 --> 00:09:59,301
where the railway leaves the city.

300
00:09:59,755 --> 00:10:00,718
It's moving.

301
00:10:00,718 --> 00:10:03,389
Slowly, the way the units move.

302
00:10:03,763 --> 00:10:05,196
Along the rails.

303
00:10:05,196 --> 00:10:06,208
Toward you.

304
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:08,636
Mara takes out the map and

305
00:10:08,636 --> 00:10:10,571
finds the line she drew on day 60.

306
00:10:10,571 --> 00:10:13,165
The place where the sky starts again.

307
00:10:13,165 --> 00:10:14,868
She smudges it with her thumb.

308
00:10:14,868 --> 00:10:16,290
In the afternoon,

309
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:18,601
two small craft pass low over the railway

310
00:10:18,601 --> 00:10:21,110
without a sound, heading for the ridge.

311
00:10:21,110 --> 00:10:23,277
You sit on the roof with the map and

312
00:10:23,277 --> 00:10:25,843
do the worst geography of your life.

313
00:10:25,843 --> 00:10:28,226
On day five, Mara asked where you'd go,

314
00:10:28,226 --> 00:10:30,263
and you said away from the ship.

315
00:10:30,263 --> 00:10:31,272
For seventy-three days,

316
00:10:31,272 --> 00:10:33,744
that's been the whole plan.

317
00:10:34,183 --> 00:10:35,697
Now, away from the ship and

318
00:10:35,697 --> 00:10:38,241
toward the mast are the same direction.

319
00:10:38,632 --> 00:10:40,040
So you go sideways.

320
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,237
Along the canal,

321
00:10:41,237 --> 00:10:44,415
away from the railway, toward neither of them.

322
00:10:44,415 --> 00:10:46,518
The boat is on their map,

323
00:10:46,518 --> 00:10:47,626
so the boat stays.

324
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:49,463
The camping stove stays too.

325
00:10:49,463 --> 00:10:52,297
Without gas, it's just a heavy memory.

326
00:10:52,817 --> 00:10:54,024
You take the kettle,

327
00:10:54,024 --> 00:10:57,706
the matches, the bottles, the lantern, the map, and the tin.

328
00:10:57,706 --> 00:10:59,415
You count the food one last

329
00:10:59,415 --> 00:11:02,093
time before it goes into the bags.

330
00:11:02,093 --> 00:11:03,637
The rice is gone.

331
00:11:03,637 --> 00:11:04,852
Five tins,

332
00:11:04,852 --> 00:11:07,766
the honey, and most of the apples.

333
00:11:07,766 --> 00:11:09,065
Eleven matches.

334
00:11:09,519 --> 00:11:11,194
Damp wood is expensive.

335
00:11:11,194 --> 00:11:12,938
You leave the ropes tied

336
00:11:12,938 --> 00:11:14,930
exactly the way you found them.

337
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,099
It's the best place

338
00:11:16,099 --> 00:11:18,148
you've ever had to leave.

339
00:11:18,148 --> 00:11:19,144
By day 81,

340
00:11:19,144 --> 00:11:22,299
the towpath has been yours for three days.

341
00:11:22,299 --> 00:11:23,936
Nothing glows.

342
00:11:23,936 --> 00:11:25,594
Nothing has been moved.

343
00:11:25,594 --> 00:11:28,302
Mara walks almost without a limp,

344
00:11:28,302 --> 00:11:30,648
and points this out about once an hour.

345
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,533
You've made one fire,

346
00:11:32,533 --> 00:11:35,009
at night, in a hollow by the water,

347
00:11:35,009 --> 00:11:37,858
and boiled as much as the kettle holds.

348
00:11:37,858 --> 00:11:40,523
In the evening, you reach a lock.

349
00:11:40,523 --> 00:11:42,333
Two heavy wooden gates hold the

350
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,440
water in a deep stone chamber,

351
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,880
with a narrow walkway along the top of

352
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,553
each and a small brick hut beside them.

353
00:11:49,553 --> 00:11:51,891
On the walkway of the near gate,

354
00:11:51,891 --> 00:11:53,467
there's a red fuel can.

355
00:11:53,467 --> 00:11:56,484
Tape on the handle, with your tiny 61.

356
00:11:56,484 --> 00:11:59,462
Mara stops so suddenly

357
00:11:59,462 --> 00:12:00,955
that you walk into her.

358
00:12:00,955 --> 00:12:01,764
For twenty days,

359
00:12:01,764 --> 00:12:03,969
that can has followed you.

360
00:12:03,969 --> 00:12:05,926
This time, it got here first.

361
00:12:05,926 --> 00:12:08,872
You came this way because you chose it,

362
00:12:08,872 --> 00:12:11,241
on a roof, with a pencil, three days ago.

363
00:12:11,566 --> 00:12:13,265
Somebody knew before you did.

364
00:12:13,265 --> 00:12:14,793
You sleep in the brick hut

365
00:12:14,793 --> 00:12:16,103
with the door shut,

366
00:12:16,103 --> 00:12:19,022
which, by now, you know proves nothing.

367
00:12:19,654 --> 00:12:21,148
Sometime after midnight,

368
00:12:21,148 --> 00:12:23,778
slow footsteps come along the towpath.

369
00:12:24,217 --> 00:12:25,485
They stop outside.

370
00:12:25,485 --> 00:12:27,288
Then there's a soft click,

371
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:30,287
and a faint pale glow appears under the door.

372
00:12:30,287 --> 00:12:32,036
Neither of you goes to look.

373
00:12:32,571 --> 00:12:33,401
On day 82,

374
00:12:33,401 --> 00:12:35,968
you open the hut door onto light.

375
00:12:35,968 --> 00:12:37,900
Two bands of it lie on the grass.

376
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:40,363
They start at the edge of the canal,

377
00:12:40,363 --> 00:12:42,354
one just past the lock and one just

378
00:12:42,354 --> 00:12:44,457
behind the hut, and run up the hill

379
00:12:44,457 --> 00:12:46,457
side by side, as far as you can see.

380
00:12:46,878 --> 00:12:47,731
Between them,

381
00:12:47,731 --> 00:12:50,405
there's a wide strip of dark grass.

382
00:12:50,405 --> 00:12:51,924
It leads up the slope.

383
00:12:51,924 --> 00:12:52,848
To the ridge.

384
00:12:52,848 --> 00:12:54,007
To the mast.

385
00:12:54,396 --> 00:12:55,978
They haven't built you a cage.

386
00:12:55,978 --> 00:12:57,758
They've built you a hallway.

387
00:12:58,163 --> 00:12:59,385
You sit on the step of the hut

388
00:12:59,385 --> 00:13:01,263
and look at the back of the map.

389
00:13:01,263 --> 00:13:02,691
Not at where you've been.

390
00:13:02,691 --> 00:13:04,090
At how you got out.

391
00:13:04,591 --> 00:13:07,080
The station: one gap, left open.

392
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,210
The store:

393
00:13:08,599 --> 00:13:11,812
one dark stretch, closing just slowly enough.

394
00:13:11,812 --> 00:13:14,161
The railway: the only line out

395
00:13:14,161 --> 00:13:15,924
of the city with no units on it,

396
00:13:15,924 --> 00:13:18,112
for exactly as long as you needed.

397
00:13:18,112 --> 00:13:19,492
The edge of the sky:

398
00:13:19,492 --> 00:13:21,845
a can, and a row of lights.

399
00:13:21,845 --> 00:13:23,529
You start to wonder how many

400
00:13:23,529 --> 00:13:25,885
of your escapes were ever yours.

401
00:13:25,885 --> 00:13:27,833
Mara isn't looking at the hallway.

402
00:13:27,833 --> 00:13:29,528
She's looking at the water.

403
00:13:29,528 --> 00:13:30,816
Both bands stop where

404
00:13:30,816 --> 00:13:32,697
the grass meets the water.

405
00:13:33,054 --> 00:13:34,604
Neither one touches it.

406
00:13:34,604 --> 00:13:35,960
You write that down,

407
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:39,126
and next to it, out of habit: observed.

408
00:13:40,590 --> 00:13:42,006
The walkway on the lock gate

409
00:13:42,006 --> 00:13:43,715
crosses the water to the far bank,

410
00:13:43,715 --> 00:13:45,462
where there's no light at all.

411
00:13:45,462 --> 00:13:48,347
Mara goes first, stepping around the can.

412
00:13:48,818 --> 00:13:50,646
The walkway is one plank wide,

413
00:13:50,646 --> 00:13:52,480
with a rail on one side,

414
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:55,278
and the water in the lock is a long way down.

415
00:13:55,650 --> 00:13:56,610
Halfway across,

416
00:13:56,610 --> 00:13:58,831
the lantern slips off your bag.

417
00:13:59,324 --> 00:14:01,170
It hits the water with a small,

418
00:14:01,170 --> 00:14:04,256
polite plop and sinks, handle first.

419
00:14:04,256 --> 00:14:05,610
You don't stop.

420
00:14:05,610 --> 00:14:07,770
You step off onto the far bank,

421
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:10,343
and the grass stays dark under your feet.

422
00:14:10,924 --> 00:14:12,925
Behind you, the hallway glows all

423
00:14:12,925 --> 00:14:16,405
the way up the hill, with nobody in it.

424
00:14:16,405 --> 00:14:17,799
For once,

425
00:14:17,799 --> 00:14:20,542
you've disappointed somebody.

426
00:14:20,542 --> 00:14:22,125
By day 85,

427
00:14:22,125 --> 00:14:25,470
you've climbed higher than you've been since the footbridge.

428
00:14:25,971 --> 00:14:28,864
Three days of woods and sheep fields,

429
00:14:28,864 --> 00:14:31,510
uphill, away from the canal.

430
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:33,681
At the top of the hill,

431
00:14:33,681 --> 00:14:35,611
there's an old sheepfold.

432
00:14:35,611 --> 00:14:37,793
A ring of dry stone wall,

433
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:42,197
chest high, with no roof and one narrow opening.

434
00:14:42,197 --> 00:14:44,433
It isn't much of a shelter.

435
00:14:44,966 --> 00:14:46,117
But from inside it,

436
00:14:46,117 --> 00:14:48,296
you can see everything coming.

437
00:14:48,814 --> 00:14:50,641
From the wall, you can see the

438
00:14:50,641 --> 00:14:53,155
whole valley you walked out of.

439
00:14:53,155 --> 00:14:54,151
The canal.

440
00:14:54,151 --> 00:14:55,058
The lock.

441
00:14:55,058 --> 00:14:56,541
The hallway,

442
00:14:56,541 --> 00:14:59,789
still glowing up the far slope, still empty.

443
00:14:59,789 --> 00:15:01,706
And at the top of it,

444
00:15:01,706 --> 00:15:03,166
on the ridge, the mast.

445
00:15:03,166 --> 00:15:05,936
For the first time, you can see its foot.

446
00:15:05,936 --> 00:15:07,583
A wide ring of pale light

447
00:15:07,583 --> 00:15:09,733
surrounds it on the ground.

448
00:15:09,733 --> 00:15:10,976
Lit paths run into it

449
00:15:10,976 --> 00:15:12,349
from three directions.

450
00:15:12,706 --> 00:15:15,138
On every path, people are walking.

451
00:15:15,138 --> 00:15:15,833
In pairs.

452
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:18,656
They arrive and stand inside the ring,

453
00:15:18,656 --> 00:15:21,337
two by two, the way people wait for a bus.

454
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:23,780
Then a small craft comes down out of the

455
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,513
sky and settles in the middle of the ring.

456
00:15:26,513 --> 00:15:27,512
No wheels.

457
00:15:27,886 --> 00:15:28,719
No sound.

458
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,553
The pairs walk to it.

459
00:15:30,553 --> 00:15:31,686
It lifts.

460
00:15:32,221 --> 00:15:35,022
It rises slowly, past the top of the mast,

461
00:15:35,022 --> 00:15:36,627
toward the straight

462
00:15:36,627 --> 00:15:37,622
dark edge of the ship,

463
00:15:37,622 --> 00:15:39,848
which now hangs over the far end of the valley.

464
00:15:39,848 --> 00:15:42,493
You watch until it's too small to see.

465
00:15:42,964 --> 00:15:44,259
From the footbridge,

466
00:15:44,259 --> 00:15:47,297
on day 42, you watched the stadium for an

467
00:15:47,297 --> 00:15:49,258
hour and never saw anyone walk out.

468
00:15:49,258 --> 00:15:50,539
Now you know why.

469
00:15:51,029 --> 00:15:52,435
They don't walk out.

470
00:15:52,435 --> 00:15:53,239
They go up.

471
00:15:53,239 --> 00:15:55,450
Mara says the word again.

472
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:56,202
Collecting.

473
00:15:56,202 --> 00:15:58,632
This time, you don't say counting.

474
00:15:59,090 --> 00:16:00,251
You don't have the heart to

475
00:16:00,251 --> 00:16:02,086
argue with what you've just watched.

476
00:16:03,427 --> 00:16:04,018
On day 88,

477
00:16:04,018 --> 00:16:06,143
the flashlight goes out for good.

478
00:16:06,459 --> 00:16:07,904
It's been dying for two months.

479
00:16:07,904 --> 00:16:10,238
You click it a few more times anyway,

480
00:16:10,238 --> 00:16:11,127
out of respect.

481
00:16:11,127 --> 00:16:13,932
The lantern is at the bottom of a lock.

482
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,047
That leaves fire,

483
00:16:15,047 --> 00:16:18,250
and fire means smoke, so most nights you go without.

484
00:16:18,250 --> 00:16:20,085
You lay out what's left on a flat

485
00:16:20,085 --> 00:16:23,074
stone in the middle of the sheepfold.

486
00:16:23,074 --> 00:16:23,622
One tin.

487
00:16:23,622 --> 00:16:24,705
Nine apples.

488
00:16:25,078 --> 00:16:26,949
The bottom of the honey jar.

489
00:16:26,949 --> 00:16:28,539
Three bottles of water.

490
00:16:28,865 --> 00:16:29,548
Seven matches.

491
00:16:29,548 --> 00:16:32,158
There's a spring at the foot of the hill,

492
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,989
but every trip down is

493
00:16:33,989 --> 00:16:35,846
a trip in plain view of the mast.

494
00:16:35,846 --> 00:16:37,030
That night,

495
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:39,543
it's cold enough that you light a fire anyway,

496
00:16:39,543 --> 00:16:41,724
small and low against the wall.

497
00:16:41,724 --> 00:16:42,783
Mara sits beside you

498
00:16:42,783 --> 00:16:44,393
with her knees pulled up.

499
00:16:44,735 --> 00:16:46,219
She asks what you'll do

500
00:16:46,219 --> 00:16:48,312
if the circles come for you.

501
00:16:48,735 --> 00:16:50,206
You think about it the way

502
00:16:50,206 --> 00:16:51,948
you think about everything now.

503
00:16:51,948 --> 00:16:54,001
Honestly, and for too long.

504
00:16:54,001 --> 00:16:55,010
Then you tell her

505
00:16:55,010 --> 00:16:56,812
they've always come for two.

506
00:16:57,248 --> 00:16:58,880
One gap at the station,

507
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,648
wide enough for two people.

508
00:17:00,648 --> 00:17:03,045
Two circles at the end of your ledger.

509
00:17:03,045 --> 00:17:05,146
Pairs, walking into the ring.

510
00:17:05,938 --> 00:17:06,838
Whatever they want,

511
00:17:06,838 --> 00:17:09,433
they've never wanted one of you without the other.

512
00:17:10,033 --> 00:17:11,413
Mara takes the pencil

513
00:17:11,413 --> 00:17:13,106
and writes it on the roll.

514
00:17:13,106 --> 00:17:13,579
Two.

515
00:17:14,129 --> 00:17:15,677
Whatever happens.

516
00:17:15,677 --> 00:17:17,226
She underlines two.

517
00:17:17,226 --> 00:17:19,100
The fire dies on its own,

518
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:20,623
a little after midnight.

519
00:17:20,623 --> 00:17:22,854
You don't light another.

520
00:17:22,854 --> 00:17:23,778
Six matches.

521
00:17:23,778 --> 00:17:26,481
On day 90, you wake to slow

522
00:17:26,481 --> 00:17:28,540
footsteps going around the sheepfold.

523
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:29,978
You know that sound.

524
00:17:30,352 --> 00:17:31,982
You know it from the store,

525
00:17:31,982 --> 00:17:35,109
and the lock, and every bad morning in between.

526
00:17:35,109 --> 00:17:36,945
You look over the wall.

527
00:17:36,945 --> 00:17:39,640
A band of pale light lies on the grass,

528
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,700
all the way around the stones.

529
00:17:42,139 --> 00:17:43,767
Then every shadow on the

530
00:17:43,767 --> 00:17:45,890
hilltop disappears at once.

531
00:17:46,329 --> 00:17:47,143
You look up.

532
00:17:47,143 --> 00:17:49,134
The straight edge is back.

533
00:17:49,604 --> 00:17:51,282
The ship is directly overhead,

534
00:17:51,282 --> 00:17:53,830
filling the sky from this hill to the mast,

535
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:56,909
the way it filled the sky over the gas station

536
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:59,313
on the evening you tried to pay for milk.

537
00:17:59,313 --> 00:18:01,826
The plain figure stands outside the band,

538
00:18:01,826 --> 00:18:03,971
on the side that faces the mast.

539
00:18:03,971 --> 00:18:05,290
Its case is closed.

540
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:07,633
The striped figure stands beside it,

541
00:18:07,633 --> 00:18:09,661
with its scanner lowered.

542
00:18:09,661 --> 00:18:11,266
Neither of them scans anything.

543
00:18:11,266 --> 00:18:12,970
They don't need to anymore.

544
00:18:13,519 --> 00:18:14,519
In front of them,

545
00:18:14,519 --> 00:18:16,019
there's a gap in the band.

546
00:18:16,019 --> 00:18:17,190
It's narrow.

547
00:18:17,190 --> 00:18:19,397
Narrower than the gap at the station.

548
00:18:19,397 --> 00:18:21,233
Narrower than the last

549
00:18:21,233 --> 00:18:23,086
dark stretch behind the store.

550
00:18:23,086 --> 00:18:25,537
Beside it, a marker begins to glow.

551
00:18:26,009 --> 00:18:26,999
One circle.

552
00:18:26,999 --> 00:18:27,742
No line.

553
00:18:27,742 --> 00:18:29,527
No second circle.

554
00:18:30,128 --> 00:18:31,065
For ninety days,

555
00:18:31,065 --> 00:18:34,176
the circles have always come in pairs.

556
00:18:34,617 --> 00:18:36,104
This one is alone.

557
00:18:36,104 --> 00:18:37,812
You look at Mara.

558
